    "text": "Discounts Lure High-Income Customers to Dollar Stores\nBy PYMNTS,\n11 hours agoHigher income consumers in the United States are crowding the aisles at dollar stores, moved to seek discounts in the paycheck-to-paycheck economy. Big box retailers such as Walmart and Target have continued to be favorites among those earnings more than $100,000 each year. But PYMNTS Intelligence data shows that higher income households are also ringing up their purchases at the likes of Dollar General and Dollar Tree.",
